WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.338
Voyage put out an update on the nineteenth of November.

4
00:00:11.338 --> 00:00:16.991
I went through it in a brand new blank world, in my Workshop world and in Voyage's own API docs.

5
00:00:16.991 --> 00:00:21.760
Three things matter if you build worlds, and the patch notes skip the second one.

6
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.614
First, combat XP.

7
00:00:24.614 --> 00:00:30.318
Under Mechanics, Advanced, Combat Settings, base combat XP is gone.

8
00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:33.553
Every NPC tier has its own reward now.

9
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.098
A brand new world gives fifty for a weak NPC,

10
00:00:37.098 --> 00:00:41.918
a hundred for an average one and a hundred and fifty for a strong one.

11
00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:48.230
Two hundred for an elite, twice that for a boss, and a thousand for a mythic.

12
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:51.351
Your old worlds were converted for you.

13
00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:55.963
Your old base became the average reward and the rest scale from it,

14
00:00:55.963 --> 00:00:59.886
so beating a boss now pays far more than any win used to.

15
00:00:59.886 --> 00:01:04.154
In episode twenty I said a win was worth a hundred by default.

16
00:01:04.154 --> 00:01:06.012
That's the average NPC now.

17
00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:12.469
These rewards are still adjusted for the level difference, and Voyage doesn't say by how much.

18
00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:15.825
Second, one the notes don't mention.

19
00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:18.980
If you edit your world as JSON or through the Creator API,

20
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.950
an NPC's starting relationship has to be called initial relationship now.

21
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.595
Voyage's own check refuses the old name, relationship, as an error.

22
00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:29.043
Your worlds in Studio were converted for you.

23
00:01:29.043 --> 00:01:33.285
It's the copies you keep yourself that need fixing, and every one of mine did.

24
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.866
Third, music has a new editor.

25
00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:39.466
Open Audio, Music, and press try it.

26
00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:42.137
Your music stays the same either way.

27
00:01:42.967 --> 00:01:48.656
Rehearse lets you type a moment the way the AI would, and shows you which theme plays.

28
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.306
And read this line.

29
00:01:50.306 --> 00:01:55.767
The AI only sees a hundred and twenty eight of your mood words, from the first themes.

30
00:01:55.767 --> 00:02:01.418
Later words still match but come up less often, so put the themes that matter most first.

31
00:02:01.867 --> 00:02:04.001
Each theme gets its own page now.

32
00:02:04.001 --> 00:02:07.751
Open one from the tree under Music, and you get its songs,

33
00:02:07.751 --> 00:02:12.083
then when it plays: its mood tags, its game moments and its places.

34
00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:16.542
Generate makes new music, and every generator costs usage.

35
00:02:16.542 --> 00:02:20.136
Lyria and Stable Audio cost about three story turns,

36
00:02:20.136 --> 00:02:24.145
the new one, Treblo, a bit more, and ElevenLabs about six.

37
00:02:24.145 --> 00:02:25.804
I don't use any of them.

38
00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:34.575
Places tie a theme to regions, locations or areas, so it usually plays while the party is there.

39
00:02:35.967 --> 00:02:37.058
The rest is quick.

40
00:02:37.058 --> 00:02:40.575
Through the Creator API you can look into player feedback,

41
00:02:40.575 --> 00:02:45.607
with the game state before or after a report and a playable link that recreates it.

42
00:02:45.607 --> 00:02:50.639
Images have to be approved and yours now, but links to your own hosting still work.

43
00:02:50.639 --> 00:02:54.034
Heal abilities and items can be made stronger or weaker,

44
00:02:54.034 --> 00:02:57.612
but there's no new setting for it, so I haven't tested how.

45
00:02:57.612 --> 00:03:00.037
And there's a new voice, a female ghost.

46
00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:06.135
That's it. My worlds and lorebooks are at deaththegrim.github.io.

47
00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.548
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

